cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite the mlumr package in publications use:'
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-only
title: 'mlumr: Multilevel Unanchored Meta-Regression for Indirect Treatment Comparisons'
version: 0.2.0
abstract: >-
  Bayesian multilevel unanchored meta-regression (ML-UMR) for indirect treatment
  comparisons using individual patient data (IPD) and aggregate data (AgD).
  Implements the shared prognostic factor assumption (SPFA) and relaxed SPFA
  models for binary, continuous, count, and time-to-event (survival) outcomes via
  Stan, including parametric and flexible M-spline survival baselines, with
  transport of marginal treatment effects to arbitrary target populations
  (covariate-conditional effects are reported at specified profiles).
  Also provides simulated treatment comparison (STC) via parametric G-computation
  and naive unadjusted benchmarks. ML-UMR is an adaptation of the multilevel
  network meta-regression (ML-NMR) methodology of Phillippo et al. (2020),
  implemented in the multinma package, to the unanchored disconnected-evidence
  setting.
